# Next.js React Rules

- Inspect the current router style before adding routes. If absent, prefer App Router for new Next.js work.
- Prefer server components and route handlers when they reduce client complexity.
- Add `use client` only where browser APIs, state, effects, or event handlers are required.
- Keep TypeScript pragmatic: avoid broad `any`; use localized escape hatches only with clear reason.
- Follow existing component and file naming conventions.
- Do not introduce a new UI library if the project already uses one.
- For forms, use the existing validation standard; if none exists, prefer Zod.
- Build responsive desktop/mobile UI for dashboard pages.
- For new dashboard UI, read existing layout, table, form, dialog, and empty-state patterns first.
